        "conclusion": "bare -fshort-wchar against newlib is not safe (these calls would reach newlib's 4-byte wchar_t implementations). A separate 16-bit code-unit type would rewrite ~586 declarations and ~398 literals and diverge from every other port. Linux and Android already use -fshort-wchar with a replacement <wchar.h> routing every wide name to 16-bit implementations (port/linux/include/wchar.h, port/linux/src/msvc_wide.c). Adopted: the same model on Wii, enforced by engine_wide_references (nm -u on every engine object)."
